{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LOOP ITERATION 10. J8 plan review round 1: BLOCK, 5 findings. All five correct; TWO of them are my\nrecurring failure mode showing up again.\n\nTHE RECURRING ONE: findings 4 and 5 were material I had ALREADY RECORDED IN THIS TICKET'S COMMENTS —\nthe port-incompleteness evidence and the RemoteRef.instance gap — and never propagated into the plan\nDESCRIPTION. The reviewer reads the description, not my comments. This is the third distinct instance\nthis session of 'I updated the analysis somewhere and left the authoritative section stale' (the other\ntwo were J9's Scope file list, twice). Recording a finding in a comment is NOT the same as planning it.\n\nFIXED:\n 1. STALE LINE REFERENCE, and the fix is instructive. The plan cited the hardcoded provenance literal\n    at apply_inbound_records.py:163. A direct read shows :163 is now an unrelated tag\n    list-comprehension; validate_creation_channel('jira') is at :211. MY OWN J9/5f48 identity fix\n    shifted it. The plan now cites the SYMBOL and says explicitly that this file has already gone\n    stale against a line number once.\n 2. ADR FILENAME was the literal placeholder 00NN. Now 0055 (0054 is taken), plus the numbering\n    caution: THREE files already share 0035, and this story amends\n    0035-reconciler-vendor-adapter-seam.md specifically. Every reference must cite the FILENAME —\n    a bare 'ADR 0035' is genuinely ambiguous in this repo.\n 3. docs/architecture.md was a Scope deliverable with NO covering AC. Now has one, and it is real\n    work: the file mentions neither reconciler.backend nor the jira-datacenter extra today.\n 4. The port-incompleteness finding is now IN THE APPROACH: 6 declared TicketTransport members vs 15\n    the core calls, 12 absent from DC, and a live crash while isinstance/contract-suite/1636 unit\n    tests were all green. The ADR must state that ADR 0035's 'the contract suite certifies a backend'\n    is CONDITIONAL on the port being complete AND typed (cc77). Epic be74 inherits this seam.\n 5. The RemoteRef.instance framing is corrected. The plan had described deployments as being\n    distinguished by it — as existing reality. It is never constructed in production code. The ADR must\n    present it as INTENDED design with the gap named and ticketed (6a91), or a future reader builds on\n    a field nothing populates. Added an AC pinning that, checkable by 'grep -rn RemoteRef( src/'\n    returning nothing.\n\nRe-review running."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785489583679903001,"uuid":"4157bbb2-fb6c-457b-94c3-43e5af43b0b9"}